    "ocr_text": "Here is the complete extraction, OCR text layout, visual typography breakdown, and design strategy analysis from the provided Instagram post image.\n\n---\n\n### **1. Post Overview & Metadata**\n* **Post URL:** [https://www.instagram.com/p/DctkvEChoLj/](https://www.instagram.com/p/DctkvEChoLj/)\n* **Post Category:** Design & Typography / Web Design & UX\n* **Core Subject:** Interactive Web Design & Hero Section Experience for \"NOMA Coffee\"\n\n---\n\n### **2. Complete Slide-by-Slide Text OCR & Breakdown**\n\n#### **Slide 1: Web Mockup View (MacBook Frame)**\n\n##### **A. Browser & Navigation Bar**\n* **Browser Tab:** `NOMA COFFEE`\n* **Address Bar URL:** `noma.studio.com/motion/`\n* **Brand Logo:** Circle icon with stylized inner letter **N** + Text: `NOMA COFFEE`\n* **Header Navigation Links:**\n  * `HOME`\n  * `ABOUT`\n  * `CONTACTS`\n  * `CONTACT`\n* **Header Icons (Right):** Search Icon (`🔍`), Favorites/Bag Icon (`🛍️`)\n\n---\n\n##### **B. Hero Section Content**\n* **Category Kicker (Sub-header):** `PREMIUM COFFEE`\n* **Main Headline:** \n  > **FOLLOW THE POUR.**\n\n* **Body Paragraph / Copy:**\n  > *\"A premium artisanal coffee experience crafting crafted coffee with fine selection, and creates every through passion and heat.\"*\n\n* **Call to Action (CTA) Controls:**\n  * Primary Button: `TASTE THE MOTION` *(Dark pill container)*\n  * Circular Icon Button: `( → )` *(Right arrow inside an outlined circle)*\n\n* **Carousel Indicator:** \n  * `— • •` *(Active line + two dots)*\n\n---\n\n##### **C. Interactive UI Controls & Visual Widgets**\n* **Right Side Vertical Scroll Control:**\n  * Top: `+`\n  * Handle: Slider pill with hand-cursor icon (`👆`)\n  * Bottom: `-`\n* **Center Bottom Overlay Widget:**\n  * Capsule control with Up/Down arrows (`▲ / ▼`)\n* **Bottom Right Quick Action Button:**\n  * Search/Floating Action Button (`🔍` inside black circle)\n\n---\n\n### **3. Design, Typography & Visual System Analysis**\n\n#### **Typography System**\n1. **Headline Font:**\n   * **Style:** High-contrast, elegant Display Serif.\n   * **Inferred Fonts:** *Playfair Display*, *Ogg*, *Baskerville*, or *Canela*.\n   * **Usage:** Used for `\"FOLLOW THE POUR.\"` to evoke luxury, quality, and craftsmanship.\n\n2. **Body & Navigation Font:**\n   * **Style:** Clean, high-legibility Sans-Serif (All Caps for Nav/Kickers).\n   * **Inferred Fonts:** *Inter*, *SF Pro Display*, or *Plus Jakarta Sans*.\n   * **Usage:** UI labels, menu items, kickers, and body copy to ensure clean digital readability.\n\n---\n\n#### **Color Palette**\n* **Background Canvas:** Soft Cream / Off-White (`#F5F2EB`)\n* **Header Banner Tone:** Muted Gold / Warm Ochre (`#C5B078`)\n* **Primary Text & Buttons:** Espresso Black (`#111111`)\n* **Hero Media Focus:** Layered Iced Matcha Coffee (Matcha Green, Milk Cream, Dark Espresso, Ice Highlights)\n\n---\n\n### **4. Key Takeaways & Interactive UX Strategy**\n\n1. **Motion-Driven E-Commerce:** Rather than static product images, the concept utilizes an interactive, scroll-triggered pour animation where the beverage responds directly to user scrolling/dragging.\n2. **Micro-Interactions Matter:** Elements like the floating directional toggle (`▲/▼`), vertical depth slider, and cursor-following icons elevate a standard hero image into an immersive experience.\n3. **Contrast Strategy:** Pairing structured modern sans-serif navigation with bold serif editorial typography creates a modern luxury aesthetic appropriate for high-end boutique brands.\n\n---\n\n### **5. Post Caption & Call to Action (CTA)**\n\n* **Caption Summary:**\n  > *\"What if the coffee didn’t just sit inside the website… but became part of the interaction? A simple pour turned into a full visual experience — built to make people stop scrolling and keep watching. Because sometimes the smallest interaction makes the biggest difference.\"*\n\n* **Lead Generation / DM Keyword:**\n  * **Keyword:** `COFFEE`\n  * **Action:** Direct message \"COFFEE\" to build custom interactive web experiences.\n* **Hashtags:** `#webdesign` `#webdevelopment` `#uidesign` `#uxdesign` `#websitedesign`",
